<title>USA: Caliber's RPS to continue service.</title>
<headline>Caliber's RPS to continue service.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>RPS Inc, a small-package ground carrier owned by Caliber Systems, said on Thursday that it will continue serving existing customers despite an increase in package volume related to a possible strike at rival United Parcel Service.</p>
<p>RPS said it had arranged plans for a controlled increase in package volume from new and existing customers as UPS renegotiated its contract with union workers.</p>
<p>On July 1, RPS announced it would not take any new customers until disputes between UPS and the Teamsters union were resolved.</p>
</text>
